1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,076
Japan is made of 14,125 islands.

2
00:00:04,657 --> 00:00:09,539
About 123 million people live on them,
from snowy mountains to tropical beaches.

3
00:00:10,044 --> 00:00:12,175
So where do you start? Let's find out.

4
00:00:12,727 --> 00:00:15,294
This is Japan, the Land of the Rising Sun.

5
00:00:16,384 --> 00:00:22,170
Four big islands hold most of the land:
Honshu, Hokkaido, Kyushu, and Shikoku.

6
00:00:23,053 --> 00:00:27,311
Together, the country covers about 378,000
square kilometers.

7
00:00:27,695 --> 00:00:29,445
But almost three quarters of it is
mountains.

8
00:00:30,035 --> 00:00:31,926
So the people crowd into the plains, which

9
00:00:31,946 --> 00:00:33,856
cover only about a quarter of the country.

10
00:00:34,444 --> 00:00:37,346
Tokyo alone has about 14 million people.

11
00:00:37,366 --> 00:00:41,164
With its neighbors, Greater Tokyo passes
30 million.

12
00:00:41,996 --> 00:00:46,474
Yokohama, Osaka, and Nagoya follow, each
with millions more.

13
00:00:47,337 --> 00:00:48,700
So let's start in Tokyo.

14
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:53,389
Neon towers, quiet shrines, and a crossing
often called the busiest in the world.

15
00:00:54,158 --> 00:00:55,746
Then hop on the Shinkansen.

16
00:00:55,766 --> 00:00:59,162
Tokyo to Kyoto takes about two hours and
fifteen minutes.

17
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:02,281
A ticket costs around 14,000 yen, roughly

18
00:01:02,301 --> 00:01:05,214
95 dollars, and trains leave every few
minutes.

19
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:11,730
Kyoto was Japan's capital for more than a
thousand years, from 794 to 1868.

20
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:14,949
Seventeen of its historic sites are World

21
00:01:14,969 --> 00:01:17,986
Heritage, from the Golden Pavilion to
quiet gardens.

22
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:20,354
Osaka is the opposite.

23
00:01:20,374 --> 00:01:23,654
Loud, hungry, and nicknamed the kitchen of
Japan.

24
00:01:24,586 --> 00:01:26,241
Now look at the extremes.

25
00:01:26,261 --> 00:01:28,786
In the north, Hokkaido gets deep snow.

26
00:01:28,806 --> 00:01:31,599
In the south, Okinawa has turquoise water.

27
00:01:31,619 --> 00:01:34,633
The country stretches about 3,000
kilometers.

28
00:01:35,317 --> 00:01:40,142
And rising above it all is Mount Fuji, at
3,776 meters.

29
00:01:41,043 --> 00:01:44,016
Japan has about 111 active volcanoes, so
natural

30
00:01:44,036 --> 00:01:47,278
hot springs, called onsen, are all over
the country.

31
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:51,235
Twenty-seven places here are UNESCO World
Heritage sites.

32
00:01:52,163 --> 00:01:53,376
Then there is the food.

33
00:01:53,396 --> 00:01:56,916
Tokyo has more Michelin starred
restaurants than any other city on

34
00:01:56,936 --> 00:01:59,993
Earth, and it has held that title for
nearly two decades.

35
00:02:00,756 --> 00:02:03,189
But you don't need a star to eat well.

36
00:02:03,209 --> 00:02:05,964
A bowl of ramen costs about 6 to 8
dollars.

37
00:02:05,984 --> 00:02:08,437
A convenience store meal, only 3 to 5.

38
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,936
A subway ride in Tokyo starts at about a
dollar twenty.

39
00:02:12,576 --> 00:02:15,764
Come in spring, and the cherry blossoms
turn whole streets pink.

40
00:02:15,784 --> 00:02:18,540
Come in winter, and the mountains
disappear under snow.

41
00:02:19,271 --> 00:02:22,937
Japan was closed to the world for 220
years.

42
00:02:22,957 --> 00:02:26,978
In 2025, a record 42 million visitors
walked in.

43
00:02:27,466 --> 00:02:30,862
Now you know why. And remember: take your
shoes off at the door.

44
00:02:31,573 --> 00:02:34,130
That was Japan. Which country should we
visit next?

45
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:35,387
Tell me in the comments.

